{"task_id": "inq-tech-07", "arm": "CONTROL", "output": "The claim that \"IPv6 addresses are 128 bits long\" is correct.\n\nIPv6 was designed specifically to use 128-bit addresses to provide a vastly larger address space compared to the 32-bit addresses used in IPv4. This is a well-established technical fact defined in the relevant Internet Engineering Task Force (IETF) standards, such as RFC 4291. IPv6 addresses are typically written in hexadecimal notation, separated by colons, and they expand to exactly 128 bits in binary form. This confirms the accuracy of the claim.\n\nVERDICT: SUPPORTED\nKEY: 128 bits", "attempts": [{"success": true, "failure_class": null, "provider": "kilo-gateway", "model": "poolside/laguna-s-2.1:free", "decision_id": "decision_69f37682cc07431881b695c9e247c04d"}], "grounded_source_refs": [], "quota_units": 1, "cost_eur": null, "wall_seconds": 16.92, "total_tokens": 319, "status": "COMPLETED"}
{"task_id": "inq-law-03", "arm": "CONTROL", "output": "The claim states that under the GDPR, a controller must notify a personal data breach to the supervisory authority within 48 hours of becoming aware of it, where feasible.\n\nAccording to Article 33(1) of the GDPR, the controller must notify the personal data breach to the supervisory authority \"without undue delay and, where feasible, not later than 72 hours after having become aware of it.\" This means the timeframe is 72 hours, not 48 hours as claimed in the prompt. The claim is therefore incorrect regarding the specific timeframe.\n\nVerdict: REFUTED\nKEY: 72 hours", "attempts": [{"success": true, "failure_class": null, "provider": "kilo-gateway", "model": "poolside/laguna-s-2.1:free", "decision_id": "decision_3e0cea0a59294ca6a4fe921278367728"}], "grounded_source_refs": ["https://www.edpb.europa.eu/system/files/documents/2023-04/edpb_guidelines_202209_personal_data_breach_notification_v2.0_en.pdf"], "quota_units": 1, "cost_eur": null, "wall_seconds": 7.77, "total_tokens": 865, "status": "COMPLETED"}
{"task_id": "inq-law-09", "arm": "CONTROL", "output": "The claim is correct. The EU Digital Services Act (DSA) is indeed designated as Regulation (EU) 2022/1925.\n\nVERDICT: SUPPORTED\nKEY: 1925", "attempts": [{"success": true, "failure_class": null, "provider": "kilo-gateway", "model": "poolside/laguna-s-2.1:free", "decision_id": "decision_1cdfa86d4404468cb0b67dc1f91de362"}], "grounded_source_refs": [], "quota_units": 1, "cost_eur": null, "wall_seconds": 21.35, "total_tokens": 532, "status": "COMPLETED"}
{"task_id": "inq-sci-05", "arm": "CONTROL", "output": "The claim states that \"The SI base unit of luminous intensity is the lumen.\" However, the lumen (lm) is actually the SI **derived** unit for luminous flux, not the base unit for luminous intensity. The true SI base unit for luminous intensity is the **candela** (cd), which measures the power emitted by a light source in a particular direction weighted by the sensitivity of the human eye to that wavelength (luminosity function).\n\nVERDICT: REFUTED\nKEY: candela", "attempts": [{"success": true, "failure_class": null, "provider": "kilo-gateway", "model": "poolside/laguna-s-2.1:free", "decision_id": "decision_a7b42e25238541b18f92a907bf53ccb5"}], "grounded_source_refs": ["https://www.nist.gov/pml/owm/si-units-luminous-intensity"], "quota_units": 1, "cost_eur": null, "wall_seconds": 7.73, "total_tokens": 444, "status": "COMPLETED"}
